<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Angelos dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1185–1204</span> · Also known as Angeloi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Angelos family ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> from 1185 to 1204 through the emperors Isaac II, Alexios III and Alexios IV. Their reign saw the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>'s capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1204. Relatives of the dynasty, calling themselves Komnenos Doukas, founded the Despotate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> and briefly the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a>.</p></div>
